WF-52 — Slack Channel Manager

## Summary

- Inputs: phone_number (or phoneNumber), name (or userName), userId
- Outputs: Returns { success, channelId, channelName, channelUrl, isNew, error? }. Creates a new private Slack channel `consult-<phoneNumber>` and invites the admin user (U0AGTECS1KR — Chinmay, single-admin MVP), OR if the channel already exists, returns the existing channel with isNew=false. On any other Slack API failure, returns { success:false, error:<reason>, channelId:null, isNew:false } so the caller can branch.
- State Transitions: none (caller — WF-22 — persists slack_channel_id to users row)
- Calls Sub-Workflows: none
- **Notes:**
  - `isNew=true` only on the freshly-created branch; `isNew=false` on name-collision recovery (used by WF-22 already-exists branch and future WF-45 rebook to skip duplicate notifications).
  - All non-`name_taken` Slack errors return `{success:false, error, channelId:null, isNew:false}` — caller must check `success` before persisting `slack_channel_id`.

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — triggered by another workflow (typically WF-22) with { phone_number, name, userId } passed through.
Step 2: Prepare channel name (code): channelName = "consult-" + phoneNumber. Carry userName, phoneNumber, userId forward. Go to Step 3.
Step 3: Create private Slack channel via Slack API (conversations.create, name=channelName, is_private=true). On error use the error output branch.
  - On success → go to Step 4 (new-channel branch).
  - On error → go to Step 6 (error branch).
Step 4: Invite admin to the new channel via Slack API (conversations.invite, channel=<new channel id>, users=['U0AGTECS1KR' /* Chinmay — single-admin MVP */]). Go to Step 5.
Step 5: Build new-channel return (code): { success:true, channelId=<new id>, channelName=<new name>, channelUrl="https://app.slack.com/client/<team_id from $env.SLACK_TEAM_ID>/<channel_id>", isNew:true }. Go to Step 10.
Step 6: Check: does the error message contain 'name_taken'?
  - If YES → go to Step 7 (recover existing channel).
  - If NO → go to Step 6a (structured error return).
Step 6a: Build error return (code): { success:false, error:<error.message>, channelId:null, channelName:channelName, channelUrl:null, isNew:false }. Go to Step 10.
Step 7: List all private channels via Slack API (conversations.list, types=private_channel, returnAll=true). Go to Step 8.
Step 8: Filter that list for the one whose name equals the prepared channelName. Go to Step 9.
Step 9: Build existing-channel return (code): { success:true, channelId=<existing id>, channelName=<existing name>, channelUrl="https://app.slack.com/client/<team_id from $env.SLACK_TEAM_ID>/<channel_id>", isNew:false }. Go to Step 10.
Step 10: End (return object emitted to caller).
